Add PROMPTS.md: the exact prompts that built this, annotated

The demo shows a BRD becoming a working app, but never showed the reader how to
do it themselves. This adds the recipe.

- Both prompts verbatim, lifted from the transcripts in iteration/ rather than
  tidied up afterwards. Verified programmatically to match byte-for-byte after
  whitespace normalisation.
- Each clause annotated with what it actually buys you, so people adapt rather
  than cargo-cult. Calls out "verify your work in a real browser before you
  finish" as the highest-value line - it is what caught all five defects.
- A fill-in-the-blanks template with four bracketed slots for someone else's BRD,
  plus a fallback for teams with no design system to point at.
- Guidance on writing the BRD so this works well: number the requirements, write
  testable rules, add a brand/visual direction section, and ask for traceability
  in the acceptance criteria.
- An honest expectations section: 20-25 minutes not seconds, it will make design
  decisions the BRD did not specify, and it is a prototype not production.

Linked from the README layout and the "how a BA actually uses this" section.

